: underline; color: #006699;" rel=3D"noopener">young people becoming detach=
ed from work</a>. But we should also recognise how long the alarm has been =
sounding. My 2008 and 2011 government reviews showed that early interventio=
n keeps people connected to work, gets them back into work and prevents tem=
porary sickness absence from becoming long-term economic inactivity. Nearly=
 two decades later, the striking fact is not that a new diagnosis has been =
found but that the old one remains and now has the added dimension of a coh=
ort of young people without work reporting high levels of mental ill health=
. Milburn is right that young people need much better training and support,=
 matched by the obligation to engage.
